      "statement": "Harness registration is modular around a ten-row harness table, artifact formats, binary selection, atomic filesystem work, state, and cleanup. It writes one Topos-owned MCP registration per ordinary harness without changing instructions or skill content; `pi` is the narrow exception that may receive a reference to an already-installed skill directory. Non-interactive installation requires explicit harnesses or `--all`, while uninstall distinguishes interactive, headless, and ambiguous-stream safety behavior.",
